  "title": "Ramesses II",
  "summary": "Ramesses II, called the Great, was a pharaoh of Egypt's Nineteenth Dynasty and son of Seti I. He fought the Hittites at the Battle of Kadesh, built temples including Abu Simbel, and founded a new capital, Pi-Ramesses. Sources date his reign 1279-1213 BCE (EBSCO) or 1304-1237 BC (an older Encyclopedia.com entry).",
